{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/838944-how-far-can-scales-of-the-dragon-go","id":838944,"title":"How far can Scales of the Dragon go?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-28T20:55:24-08:00","id":838944,"title":"How far can Scales of the Dragon go?","content":"I was wondering, what's the limit on how much a Scale of the Dragon can alter a vampire? I know each one has to have a cost, but what's the maximum level of power? How far can it go into full-on body modification. <br /> <br /> For example, I saw an old thread on homebrew Scales that included implanting a plate of armor into the vampire's body. I was wondering if, for example, a vampire could implant a hidden firearm into her arm? A retractable blade? A taser?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T21:54:50-08:00","id":838962,"title":"","content":"As far as you are comfortable going in your games. But never far enough for the vampire using them.<br /> <br /> But, as for implanted firearms I think that'd be well within the range of scales, yes. Perhaps just a standard merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T22:00:52-08:00","id":838965,"title":"","content":"Personally, my limit would be surgically removing part of your Beast in the form of a Shadow Potency 1 Strix, using your Dirge in place of a Vice. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YW_3GLIeXi4\" target=\"_blank\">With <i>sexy</i> results</a>.<br /> <br /> No, this isn't overly specific, why do you ask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T06:33:19-08:00","id":839118,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't bother with a Scale for the implants. There's nothing mystical going on there. There's no real advantage, and likely a whole lot of problems blending in with society by turning yourself into a cyborg. I mean, hells. Its more effective to hide weapons with Obfuscate than trying to go all robocop. And I'm pretty sure there's some major powers that can be used to protect your heart with some drawbacks, so I don't think its too much of an issue here. Metal plates are messy, since they need to 1) somehow be made permanent, 2) you still need to breath to talk, which requires chest expanding and not something metal plates are really designed to allow, and 3) if it becomes common knowledge, someone trying to take you down isn't going to bother with the easy way of holding you in torpor. You'll be lucky if they merely reach for more brutal methods of holding you down. <br /> <br /> I'd give some kinds of social penalties, because to be honest, its not scientifically possible without looking like something is off about you. And it definitely would be a Humanity sin to do it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the limits of Scales in general? I'd allow them to be as powerful as any other Coil. In my mind, Scales are merely glorified &quot;Coil Devotions&quot; and can be as powerful as any Devotion on the market, even Elder ones, but limited to the Mystery's theme. Really, the theme of the associated Coil is the big limit in my mind. Anything else, assuming appropriate costs and difficulties, should be fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T07:11:47-08:00","id":839139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/838944-how-far-can-scales-of-the-dragon-go?p=838965#post838965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, my limit would be surgically removing part of your Beast in the form of a Shadow Potency 1 Strix, using your Dirge in place of a Vice. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YW_3GLIeXi4\" target=\"_blank\">With <i>sexy</i> results</a>.<br /> <br /> No, this isn't overly specific, why do you ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make it shadow potency = victim's BP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:05:06-08:00","id":839343,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm, how would it work as a Merit? You really think a vampire could just make themselves a cyborg without having to use mystical hoohah? How well does Protean work when you have a giant chunk of metal in you?<br /> <br /> In terms of cost, I'm thinking that the vampire needs to take damage to bring the weapon out, since it has to tear out of their flesh to expose the barrel. <br /> <br /> How about grafting on extra limbs? Y'know, going full Centimani?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T12:18:54-08:00","id":839354,"title":"","content":"Never go full Centimani.<br /> <br /> Joking aside, that sounds almost like a Protean Devotion. Maybe a Scale to make Protean changes (or other, if available) long term/permanent? The Kindred condition already has slight precedent in using willpower to prevent minor alterations (scars, tattoos, etc.) from reverting during the daysleep. A Scale might work off that to supercharge it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}